          (uuid "7627603a-6462-5977-8a03-943f7418fc7c"))
(text "Design basis: examples/sic-buck-400v-200v-5kw/design/design_decisions.json (schema 3, 2026-10-10) - single source of truth; electrical model automation/kicad_tools/sic_buck_power_model.py; generator automation/kicad_tools/generate_sic_schematics.py.\n400 V (360-440 V) to 200 V / 25 A / 5 kW / 50 kHz synchronous buck; Wolfspeed C4MS025120K; TMS320F28335 control board on a stacked SELV mezzanine.\nNet classes: HV_VIN, HV_SW, HV_PGND, HV_VOUT, DRV_HS, DRV_LS, DESAT_HS, DESAT_LS, SENSE_ISO - HV classes 3 mm, driver / DESAT / sensing islands 0.3 mm intra-class, PE 5 mm, CTRL_SELV and Default 0.25 mm (70 um copper).\nBoard rules (.kicad_dru): HV side to CTRL_SELV 9 mm on all layers; HV to PE 5 mm; HV functional 3 mm outer / 1 mm inner; HV to board edge 1 mm; 36 pin-field exceptions derived from pad geometry (9 barrier, 19 HV, 8 package pitch) - creepage review.\nBarrier parts (UCC21710 x2, UCC14141 x3, AMC1311 x2, TMCS1133) need the 1.2 mm non-plated isolation slot of the baseline; the custom AIPE footprints embed it, the UCC21710 library footprint does not (layout task).\nTO-247-4 pad order 1 D, 2 S, 3 KS, 4 G is an ASSUMPTION (Wolfspeed PRD 05966 front view); unverified parts and placeholders are listed in components/bom_power.csv notes and in the model docstring.\nEvidence: native ERC manifests under verification/erc/<run>/run.json; review PDF under review/; this drawing has no CAD evidence beyond those runs. AI-GENERATED ENGINEERING PROTOTYPE - V2 - HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED." (at 20 31 0)
          (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
          (uuid "b4f97cd2-46b2-5740-a698-f4e122ea5ff1"))
